Turns on local email/password auth (already scaffolded but disabled) and
wires it up end-to-end.

- app-env.json / .grok/app-env.json: VITE_AUTH_ENABLED → "true"
- src/lib/auth/email-password.ts: emailAndPasswordEnabled → true
- src/routes/api/auth/$.ts: new — mounts the existing Better Auth
  instance (src/lib/auth/server.ts) at /api/auth/*
- src/routes/login.tsx: new — email/password sign-up + sign-in form,
  redirects to / on success or if already signed in
- src/components/app-shell.tsx: header shows Sign in (signed out) or
  the account chip + sign-out (signed in)
- src/routeTree.gen.ts: regenerated by `vite build` to include the
  two new routes

No Grok OAuth UI added to /login per AGENTS.md (those buttons are
reserved for the app-data skill's login-error state, not a general
sign-in page).

Deploy note: real (non-preview) email/password persistence needs
DATABASE_URL + BETTER_AUTH_SECRET set on the host — project/env
config, not part of this diff.
